  "contracts": [
    "The service viewport callback explicitly refreshes shared action visible bounds before scheduling scene projection. This cancels interactions on clipped controls; all other scene refresh calls remain unchanged.",
    "A regression inside the real 80-download scene presses the first Reveal action, asserts its pressed state, scrolls it fully offscreen and verifies the pressed state is cancelled. No Reveal/file/Finder action is executed by the regression. Existing scene clipping, dark theme, synchronous close/editor teardown, reopen and profile-isolation checks remain.",
    "The callback retains its weak PanelScene lifetime binding. The content-root adapter is owned by the same widget subtree and cleared by existing scene-before-widget teardown.",
